{
  "sn22.3:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.3 ",
  "sn22.3:0.2": "1. Nakula’s Father ",
  "sn22.3:0.3": "With Hāliddikāni ",
  "sn22.3:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn22.3:1.2": "At one time Venerable Mahākaccāna was staying in the land of the Avantis near Kuraraghara on Steep Mountain. ",
  "sn22.3:1.3": "Then the householder Hāliddikāni went up to Venerable Mahākaccāna, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "sn22.3:1.4": "“Sir, this was said by the Buddha in the Chapter of the Eights, in ‘The Questions of Māgandiya’: ",
  "sn22.3:2.1": "‘After leaving their bastion to migrate without abode, ",
  "sn22.3:2.2": "a sage doesn’t get close to anyone in town. ",
  "sn22.3:2.3": "Rid of sensual pleasures, not expecting, ",
  "sn22.3:2.4": "they wouldn’t get in arguments with people.’ ",
  "sn22.3:3.1": "How should we see the detailed meaning of the Buddha’s brief statement?” ",
  "sn22.3:4.1": "“Householder, the form element is a bastion for consciousness. ",
  "sn22.3:4.2": "One whose consciousness is shackled by greed for the form element is called a migrant going from bastion to bastion. ",
  "sn22.3:4.3": "The feeling element is a bastion for consciousness. ",
  "sn22.3:4.4": "One whose consciousness is shackled to greed for the feeling element is called a migrant going from bastion to bastion. ",
  "sn22.3:4.5": "The perception element is a bastion for consciousness. ",
  "sn22.3:4.6": "One whose consciousness is shackled to greed for the perception element is called a mi